// The package runner is the design model of the live machine runner, std
// actor.StartMachine (runtime.md, Machines and actors 11 to 13; runtime/v1
// actor.go, rules 1 to 8, 11 and 17), checked by `ergo test models/runner`.
// It replaced the Quint model actor_machine.qnt of
// docs/research/actor-machine (MU3, MU4, MU12, fua-a; deleted): the same
// actions and invariants, decided by a breadth-first search of every state
// in a small scope instead of random traces (wf10 explorer X4).
//
// Senders admit signals into one inbox of capacity Cap: a Send, or an Ask
// that waits for its answer. The runner takes the front envelope and steps
// it to completion before it takes the next (run to completion). Each
// entry of the machine (the first state, an Enter, an Emit) may arm one
// timer: a child that sleeps and then pushes a timer envelope tagged with
// its entry's epoch into the same inbox. When an entry ends, the runner
// stops the timer child and waits until it has ended before the next entry
// arms its own (exit before entry); a timer envelope of an ended entry
// that is already in the inbox is dropped, never stepped. Done ends the
// actor: the inbox closes, queued Asks are answered Stopped, and nothing is
// stepped after it. Stop (from outside) closes admission, interrupts the
// runner (an Ask in flight is answered Stopped) and drains the inbox the
// same way. The step's decision is a free choice in every step.
//
// The entry's work (MU4) is a second child of the entry, started after the
// commit and before observers see the new state. A running work pushes
// result envelopes tagged with its entry's epoch (one and it ends, or one
// of a listener's, which goes on), or one defect envelope, which ends the
// actor whatever its epoch. When the entry ends, the runner interrupts the
// work and waits for its end before the next entry starts its own; an
// interrupted work pushes nothing.
//
// Observers and the drain (MU12): each observer may begin a
// Changes loop at any point; it gets the state shown now, then each state
// published after it, from a buffer of its own, and its loop ends once the
// actor ended and it read the buffer. Every written state is published: a
// Stay's at its commit, an entry's once its children run, and one whose
// entry a stop overtook at the halt. Drain closes admission; the runner
// steps what is queued and ends when nothing is queued and no entry is
// open. An Emit's output goes to the sink with the commit that gives it
// (fua-a), so no observer is shown a state that owes its output.
//
// Each action of the Quint model is a signal; an action that is not
// enabled is Ignore. The model starts in Boot; Start chooses whether the
// first entry has a timer and a work (Quint's init). The invariants are
// checked after each step: a step that breaks one enters Broken with its
// name. RunToCompletion, NoStaleStep, ExitBeforeEntry, OneTimerPerEntry,
// OneLiveWorkPerEntry, TimerOnlyInItsEntry, WorkOnlyInItsEntry,
// NothingAfterInterrupt, ObserversAfterWork, NoStepAfterEnd,
// PerSenderOrder, AskAnsweredOnce, ChangesInOrderOnce,
// WaitForMatchesReplay, NothingAfterEnd, DrainStepsQueued and
// OutputBeforeShown are the Quint model's (see holds).
//
// The scope is the Quint model's (2 senders of 2 signals each, and 3 in
// Design3; an inbox of 2; observers, see below), with one bound Quint has as its 40
// steps: at most MaxWrites commits (Enter, Stay, Emit), so at most
// MaxWrites entries after the first. It is the claim: "proved" means
// proved in this scope. The state is the Quint state with what no action
// or invariant can tell apart merged (each is exact: two merged states have
// the same futures and the same verdicts):
//
//   - an Ask leaves the system once (stepped, drained, refused), answered
//     or not, so the answers per id are Twice (an Ask answered twice) and
//     Lost (an Ask left unanswered);
//   - a signal leaves the inbox by a take or by a drop, so "the drain
//     stepped every signal it admitted" is "no admitted signal was
//     dropped" (Dropped);
//   - the timer and work counts per entry: only the current entry's can
//     grow, so ArmsNow and StartsNow count the current entry's, and
//     ArmsBad and StartsBad keep an older entry's past 1;
//   - an observer's states read are, in a state that breaks nothing,
//     consecutive from its start, so it keeps Next (the state it must read
//     next) and Read (whether it read one);
//   - epochs are relative: an epoch only grows, and every action and
//     invariant only compares an epoch with the current one, so an epoch
//     is "current" (0) or "ended" (-1), and Quint's epoch counter goes;
//   - the senders are symmetric, so they are relabeled to a canonical
//     order (canon);
//   - a field that no later action reads is cleared: the timer's and the
//     work's entry when they are none, the epoch of a defect and of a
//     sender's envelope, the sender and number of the envelope in the step
//     (read only at its take);
//   - one observer stands for Quint's two: an observer's actions change
//     only its own record and never enable or disable another action, and
//     each invariant and witness over observers is about one observer, so a
//     run with two observers, less one observer's actions, is a run with
//     one, with the same verdicts;
//   - counters that only the witnesses read (asks, admitted signals, an
//     observer's reads, the states an Emit wrote) are kept only by the
//     witness machine that reads it (Ghost).
//
// Mutants, each a machine whose law Breaks must hold (a shortest run that
// breaks the invariant named; as in the Quint check, each mutant machine
// checks only that one):
//   - NoEpoch: the runner steps a timer envelope without its epoch check
//     (NoStaleStep);
//   - ArmEarly: the next entry arms before the old timer child ended
//     (ExitBeforeEntry);
//   - StayRestarts: Stay restarts the timer, as an Enter does
//     (OneTimerPerEntry);
//   - NoClose: Done does not close the inbox; the runner goes on
//     (NoStepAfterEnd);
//   - AnswerTwice: an Ask is answered twice (AskAnsweredOnce);
//   - TwoAtOnce: the runner takes a second envelope while one is in a step
//     (RunToCompletion);
//   - AnyOrder: the runner takes any envelope, not the front one
//     (PerSenderOrder);
//   - NoWorkEpoch: the runner steps a result envelope of an ended entry
//     (NoStaleStep);
//   - WorkEarly: the next entry's work starts before the old work ended
//     (ExitBeforeEntry);
//   - FailOnInterrupt: an interrupted work pushes its failure
//     (NothingAfterInterrupt);
//   - WorkBeforeCommit: the work starts with the epoch before the commit
//     (WorkOnlyInItsEntry);
//   - PublishFirst: observers see the new entry before its work starts
//     (ObserversAfterWork);
//   - NotifyTwice: an observer reads a state and keeps it, so it gets it
//     twice (ChangesInOrderOnce);
//   - SkipBeforeStop: an observer's loop ends at the end with states unread
//     (NothingAfterEnd);
//   - StaleSnapshot: a new observer's first state is one from before its
//     start (WaitForMatchesReplay);
//   - DrainDrops: Drain drops the last queued signal (DrainStepsQueued);
//   - OutputLate: an Emit's output goes to the sink after its entry is
//     shown, the runner before fua-a (OutputBeforeShown).
//
// Witnesses, each a machine whose law Reached must hold, so the invariants
// are not vacuous: a stale tick and a stale result in a step; an
// interrupted work; a defect in a step; the end after two Asks with every
// sender done; a full inbox; two senders queued; an observer that read
// three states to the end; a wait begun after two commits; a stop that ends
// the actor while an observer has states unread; a drain that ends the
// actor after two admitted signals; an observer that reads a state an Emit
// wrote.
//
// Workarounds of today's Ergo: a variant with no fields is written `S0{}`
// in its union; there is no slice update expression, so setInt, setBool
// and setObs copy a slice.

type Sender = S0{} | S1{} | S2{}

type Ob = O0{}

// At is the index of the envelope a take picks (AnyOrder only; the
// design takes the front).
type At = At0{} | At1{}

// Dec is the step's decision.
type Dec = DEnter{} | DStay{} | DEmit{} | DIgnore{} | DReject{} | DDone{}

// Env is an envelope. Kind is Send, Ask, Tick, Result, Defect or NoKind; a
// tick, a result and a defect have Sender -1 and Seq 0; Epoch is 0 when the
// envelope is of the current entry and -1 when its entry ended (a tick or a
// result; 0 for the others). The envelope in the step keeps its kind and
// its epoch only.
type Env { Kind int, Sender int, Seq int, Epoch int }

// Obs is an observer: whether it subscribed, the state it must read next,
// whether it read one, its reads (a witness counter, up to 3), the states
// published to it that it has not read, and whether its loop ended.
type Obs { Sub bool, Next int, Read bool, Count int, Buf []int, Done bool }

// World is the Quint model's state, merged as the header says. Runner is
// Idle, Busy or Ended; Timer and Work are NoChild, Sleeping (Running) or
// Stopping; EndBy is how the actor ended (NotEnded, ByDone, ByDefect,
// ByStop, ByDrain). TimerEpoch and WorkEpoch are 0 for the current entry
// and -1 for an ended one; Seen is -1 when observers were last shown an
// ended entry, 0 the current one, as Quint's seen against epoch.
type World {
	Inbox       []Env,
	NextSeq     []int,
	Open        bool,
	StopReq     bool,
	Runner      int,
	Cur         Env,
	InFlight    int,
	Timer       int,
	TimerEpoch  int,
	Work        int,
	WorkEpoch   int,
	Pending     bool,
	Seen        int,
	ArmsNow     int,
	ArmsBad     bool,
	StartsNow   int,
	StartsBad   bool,
	LastStepped []int,
	Twice       bool,
	Lost        bool,
	StaleBad    bool,
	ArmEarly    bool,
	WorkEarly   bool,
	AfterIntr   bool,
	AfterEnd    bool,
	OrderBad    bool,
	DoneSeen    bool,
	ChangesBad  bool,
	WaitForBad  bool,
	State       int,
	Shown       int,
	Obs         []Obs,
	Owed        []int,
	DrainReq    bool,
	EndBy       int,
	Dropped     bool,
	Asked       int,
	Admitted    int,
	Emits       []bool,
}

// St is the model's state: Boot before Start, the world, a broken
// invariant, or a witness reached (only the witness machines enter Seen).
type St = Boot{} | Live{W World} | Broken{Why string} | Seen{What string}

// Act is the actions of the Quint model, and Start, its init.
type Act = Start{Timer bool, Work bool} | Admit{S Sender, Ask bool} | Fire{} | TimerEnds{} | WorkPush{Defect bool, Last bool} | WorkEnds{} | Take{At At} | Drop{} | DefectEnds{} | StepIt{D Dec} | Arm{Timer bool, Work bool} | RequestStop{} | Halt{} | Subscribe{O Ob} | Observe{O Ob} | ObserverEnds{O Ob} | RequestDrain{} | DrainEnds{} | GiveOut{}

// The scope.
let Msgs = 2
let Cap = 2
let MaxWrites = 2

// Envelope kinds.
let Send = 0
let Ask = 1
let Tick = 2
let Result = 3
let Defect = 4
let NoKind = 5

// The runner, the timer and the work.
let Idle = 0
let Busy = 1
let Ended = 2
let NoChild = 0
let Sleeping = 1
let Running = 1
let Stopping = 2

// How the actor ended.
let NotEnded = 0
let ByDone = 1
let ByDefect = 2
let ByStop = 3
let ByDrain = 4

// The mutants and the design, as the argument of next.
let NoMutant = 0
let NoEpochMutant = 1
let ArmEarlyMutant = 2
let StayRestartsMutant = 3
let NoCloseMutant = 4
let AnswerTwiceMutant = 5
let TwoAtOnceMutant = 6
let AnyOrderMutant = 7
let NoWorkEpochMutant = 8
let WorkEarlyMutant = 9
let FailOnInterruptMutant = 10
let WorkBeforeCommitMutant = 11
let PublishFirstMutant = 12
let NotifyTwiceMutant = 13
let SkipBeforeStopMutant = 14
let StaleSnapshotMutant = 15
let DrainDropsMutant = 16
let OutputLateMutant = 17

// The invariants, in the order broken checks them.
let Invariants = []string{"RunToCompletion", "NoStaleStep", "ExitBeforeEntry", "OneTimerPerEntry", "OneLiveWorkPerEntry", "TimerOnlyInItsEntry", "WorkOnlyInItsEntry", "NothingAfterInterrupt", "ObserversAfterWork", "NoStepAfterEnd", "PerSenderOrder", "AskAnsweredOnce", "ChangesInOrderOnce", "WaitForMatchesReplay", "NothingAfterEnd", "DrainStepsQueued", "OutputBeforeShown"}

// Cfg is a machine of the model: its mutant, its number of senders, the
// witness whose counter it keeps (0: none), and the invariant it checks
// ("": every one).
type Cfg { M int, Senders int, Ghost int, Only string }

func senderIx(s Sender) int {
	match s {
	case S0:
		0
	case S1:
		1
	case S2:
		2
	}
}

func obIx(o Ob) int {
	match o {
	case O0:
		0
	}
}

func atIx(a At) int {
	match a {
	case At0:
		0
	case At1:
		1
	}
}

func setInt(xs []int, i int, v int) []int {
	let mut out = []int{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j == i {
			out = out.Append(v)
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

func setBool(xs []bool, i int, v bool) []bool {
	let mut out = []bool{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j == i {
			out = out.Append(v)
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

func setObs(xs []Obs, i int, v Obs) []Obs {
	let mut out = []Obs{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j == i {
			out = out.Append(v)
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

func removeAt(xs []Env, i int) []Env {
	let mut out = []Env{}
	for j, x in xs {
		if j != i {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

// aged is the inbox after its entry ended: each tick and result in it is
// of an ended entry.
func aged(xs []Env) []Env {
	let mut out = []Env{}
	for x in xs {
		if x.Kind == Tick || x.Kind == Result {
			out = out.Append(Env{..x, Epoch: -1})
		} else {
			out = out.Append(x)
		}
	}
	out
}

func noEnv() Env {
	Env{Kind: NoKind, Sender: -1, Seq: -1, Epoch: -1}
}

func noObs() Obs {
	Obs{Sub: false, Next: 0, Read: false, Count: 0, Buf: []int{}, Done: false}
}

func isSignal(e Env) bool {
	e.Kind == Send || e.Kind == Ask
}

// hasSignal reports whether the inbox holds a sender's signal.
func hasSignal(xs []Env) bool {
	for x in xs {
		if isSignal(x) {
			return true
		}
	}
	false
}

// first is the start, before Quint's init.
func first() St {
	Boot
}

// booted is the state after Quint's init: the first entry with its timer
// and its work, or none.
func booted(timer bool, work bool) World {
	World{
		Inbox:       []Env{},
		NextSeq:     []int{0, 0, 0},
		Open:        true,
		StopReq:     false,
		Runner:      Idle,
		Cur:         noEnv(),
		InFlight:    0,
		Timer:       if timer { Sleeping } else { NoChild },
		TimerEpoch:  0,
		Work:        if work { Running } else { NoChild },
		WorkEpoch:   0,
		Pending:     false,
		Seen:        0,
		ArmsNow:     if timer { 1 } else { 0 },
		ArmsBad:     false,
		StartsNow:   if work { 1 } else { 0 },
		StartsBad:   false,
		LastStepped: []int{-1, -1, -1},
		Twice:       false,
		Lost:        false,
		StaleBad:    false,
		ArmEarly:    false,
		WorkEarly:   false,
		AfterIntr:   false,
		AfterEnd:    false,
		OrderBad:    false,
		DoneSeen:    false,
		ChangesBad:  false,
		WaitForBad:  false,
		State:       0,
		Shown:       0,
		Obs:         []Obs{noObs()},
		Owed:        []int{},
		DrainReq:    false,
		EndBy:       NotEnded,
		Dropped:     false,
		Asked:       0,
		Admitted:    0,
		Emits:       []bool{false, false, false, false},
	}
}

// sendersDone reports whether every sender of the scope sent its signals.
func sendersDone(c Cfg, w World) bool {
	for i in 0..c.Senders {
		if w.NextSeq[i] < Msgs {
			return false
		}
	}
	true
}

// holds reports whether w keeps the invariant name.
func holds(c Cfg, w World, name string) bool {
	if name == "RunToCompletion" {
		return w.InFlight <= 1
	}
	if name == "NoStaleStep" {
		return !w.StaleBad
	}
	if name == "ExitBeforeEntry" {
		return !w.ArmEarly && !w.WorkEarly
	}
	if name == "OneTimerPerEntry" {
		return !w.ArmsBad && w.ArmsNow <= 1
	}
	if name == "OneLiveWorkPerEntry" {
		return !w.StartsBad && w.StartsNow <= 1
	}
	if name == "TimerOnlyInItsEntry" {
		return w.Timer != Sleeping || w.TimerEpoch == 0 || w.Pending
	}
	if name == "WorkOnlyInItsEntry" {
		return w.Work != Running || w.WorkEpoch == 0 || w.Pending
	}
	if name == "NothingAfterInterrupt" {
		return !w.AfterIntr
	}
	if name == "ObserversAfterWork" {
		return !(w.Pending && w.Seen == 0)
	}
	if name == "NoStepAfterEnd" {
		return !w.AfterEnd
	}
	if name == "PerSenderOrder" {
		return !w.OrderBad
	}
	if name == "AskAnsweredOnce" {
		return !w.Twice && !(w.Runner == Ended && sendersDone(c, w) && w.Lost)
	}
	if name == "ChangesInOrderOnce" {
		return !w.ChangesBad
	}
	if name == "WaitForMatchesReplay" {
		return !w.WaitForBad
	}
	if name == "NothingAfterEnd" {
		for o in w.Obs {
			if o.Done && !(w.Runner == Ended && o.Read && o.Next-1 == w.State) {
				return false
			}
		}
		return true
	}
	if name == "DrainStepsQueued" {
		return w.EndBy != ByDrain || !w.Dropped
	}
	// OutputBeforeShown: no state an observer is shown, or may read, owes
	// its output.
	for i in w.Owed {
		if i <= w.Shown {
			return false
		}
	}
	true
}

// broken is the name of the first invariant w breaks among those c checks,
// or "".
func broken(c Cfg, w World) string {
	for name in Invariants {
		if (c.Only == "" || c.Only == name) && !holds(c, w, name) {
			return name
		}
	}
	""
}

// publish shows the state s to every subscribed observer whose loop has
// not ended.
func publish(w World, s int) World {
	let mut obs = []Obs{}
	for o in w.Obs {
		if o.Sub && !o.Done {
			obs = obs.Append(Obs{..o, Buf: o.Buf.Append(s)})
		} else {
			obs = obs.Append(o)
		}
	}
	World{..w, Shown: s, Obs: obs}
}

// showWritten publishes the last written state if it is not shown yet.
func showWritten(w World) World {
	if w.Shown != w.State {
		return publish(w, w.State)
	}
	w
}

// stopChildren asks the timer child to stop and interrupts the work.
func stopChildren(w World) World {
	World{..w,
		Timer: if w.Timer == Sleeping { Stopping } else { w.Timer },
		Work:  if w.Work == Running { Stopping } else { w.Work },
	}
}

// answered is w after the Ask e (if it is one) got n answers.
func answered(w World, e Env, n int) World {
	if e.Kind == Ask && n >= 2 {
		return World{..w, Twice: true}
	}
	w
}

// drained is w after the queued envelopes were cleared at an end: every
// queued Ask is answered Stopped, and each queued signal is dropped.
func drained(w World) World {
	World{..w, Inbox: []Env{}, Dropped: w.Dropped || hasSignal(w.Inbox)}
}

// Perms2 and Perms3 are the relabelings of 2 and 3 senders: p[i] is the
// new label of sender i.
let Perms2 = [][]int{[]int{0, 1, 2}, []int{1, 0, 2}}
let Perms3 = [][]int{[]int{0, 1, 2}, []int{0, 2, 1}, []int{1, 0, 2}, []int{1, 2, 0}, []int{2, 0, 1}, []int{2, 1, 0}}

// relabel is w with sender i named p[i].
func relabel(w World, p []int) World {
	let mut nextSeq = []int{0, 0, 0}
	let mut last = []int{0, 0, 0}
	for i in 0..3 {
		nextSeq = setInt(nextSeq, p[i], w.NextSeq[i])
		last = setInt(last, p[i], w.LastStepped[i])
	}
	let mut inbox = []Env{}
	for e in w.Inbox {
		inbox = inbox.Append(if e.Sender >= 0 { Env{..e, Sender: p[e.Sender]} } else { e })
	}
	World{..w, NextSeq: nextSeq, LastStepped: last, Inbox: inbox}
}

// senderKey is what a relabeling changes, so two relabelings of w with one
// key are one state.
func senderKey(w World) []int {
	let mut k = []int{}
	for i in 0..3 {
		k = k.Append(w.NextSeq[i])
		k = k.Append(w.LastStepped[i])
	}
	for e in w.Inbox {
		k = k.Append(e.Sender)
	}
	k
}

func lessInts(a []int, b []int) bool {
	for i, x in a {
		if x != b[i] {
			return x < b[i]
		}
	}
	false
}

// canon is w in its canonical form: the senders relabeled to the least
// key (the senders are symmetric: each sends the same signals, and every
// invariant and witness reads them alike), and the entries of a timer or
// a work that is none cleared.
func canon(c Cfg, v World) World {
	let perms = if c.Senders == 3 { Perms3 } else { Perms2 }
	let mut w = v
	let mut key = senderKey(v)
	for p in perms {
		let r = relabel(v, p)
		let k = senderKey(r)
		if lessInts(k, key) {
			w = r
			key = k
		}
	}
	World{..w,
		TimerEpoch: if w.Timer == NoChild { 0 } else { w.TimerEpoch },
		WorkEpoch:  if w.Work == NoChild { 0 } else { w.WorkEpoch },
	}
}

// stale reports whether the envelope in the step is a tick or a result of
// an ended entry that the runner drops (NoEpoch steps a stale tick,
// NoWorkEpoch a stale result).
func stale(c Cfg, w World) bool {
	(w.Cur.Kind == Tick && w.Cur.Epoch != 0 && c.M != NoEpochMutant) || (w.Cur.Kind == Result && w.Cur.Epoch != 0 && c.M != NoWorkEpochMutant)
}

// next is w after the action a in the machine c, or None when a is not
// enabled.
func next(c Cfg, w World, a Act) Option[World] {
	match a {
	case Start:
		None
	case Admit as ad:
		// A sender admits its next signal, or is refused Stopped once
		// admission closed (a refused Ask is answered by the refusal).
		let i = senderIx(ad.S)
		if i >= c.Senders || w.NextSeq[i] >= Msgs {
			return None
		}
		let e = Env{Kind: if ad.Ask { Ask } else { Send }, Sender: i, Seq: w.NextSeq[i], Epoch: 0}
		let asked = if c.Ghost == EndAfterAsksWitness && ad.Ask && w.Asked < 2 { w.Asked + 1 } else { w.Asked }
		let w2 = World{..w, NextSeq: setInt(w.NextSeq, i, w.NextSeq[i]+1), Asked: asked}
		if !w.Open {
			return Some[World]{Value: w2}
		}
		if len(w.Inbox) >= Cap {
			return None
		}
		let admitted = if c.Ghost == DrainEndWitness && w.Admitted < 2 { w.Admitted + 1 } else { w.Admitted }
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w2, Inbox: w.Inbox.Append(e), Admitted: admitted}}
	case Fire:
		// The timer child wakes and pushes its tick, with its entry's
		// epoch; a child asked to stop may still push (a stale tick).
		if (w.Timer != Sleeping && w.Timer != Stopping) || !w.Open || len(w.Inbox) >= Cap {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Inbox: w.Inbox.Append(Env{Kind: Tick, Sender: -1, Seq: 0, Epoch: w.TimerEpoch}), Timer: NoChild}}
	case TimerEnds:
		// A stopped timer child ends without pushing.
		if w.Timer != Stopping {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Timer: NoChild}}
	case WorkPush as p:
		// A running work pushes a result with its entry's epoch (the last,
		// or one of a listener's), or a defect, and ends. An interrupted
		// work pushes nothing (FailOnInterrupt: it pushes its failure).
		if !(w.Work == Running || (c.M == FailOnInterruptMutant && w.Work == Stopping)) || !w.Open || len(w.Inbox) >= Cap {
			return None
		}
		let k = if p.Defect { Defect } else { Result }
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w,
			Inbox:     w.Inbox.Append(Env{Kind: k, Sender: -1, Seq: 0, Epoch: if p.Defect { 0 } else { w.WorkEpoch }}),
			Work:      if p.Last || p.Defect { NoChild } else { w.Work },
			AfterIntr: w.AfterIntr || w.Work == Stopping,
		}}
	case WorkEnds:
		// A work ends: a listener returns with nothing to send, or an
		// interrupted work ends without pushing.
		if w.Work != Running && w.Work != Stopping {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Work: NoChild}}
	case Take as t:
		// The runner takes the front envelope (AnyOrder: any one;
		// TwoAtOnce: also while one is in a step).
		let k = atIx(t.At)
		if !(w.Runner == Idle || (c.M == TwoAtOnceMutant && w.Runner == Busy)) || w.Pending || w.StopReq || len(w.Inbox) == 0 {
			return None
		}
		if k >= len(w.Inbox) || (k > 0 && c.M != AnyOrderMutant) {
			return None
		}
		let e = w.Inbox[k]
		let signal = isSignal(e)
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w,
			Cur:         Env{..e, Sender: -1, Seq: -1},
			Inbox:       removeAt(w.Inbox, k),
			OrderBad:    w.OrderBad || (signal && e.Seq < w.LastStepped[e.Sender]),
			LastStepped: if signal { setInt(w.LastStepped, e.Sender, e.Seq) } else { w.LastStepped },
			Runner:      Busy,
			InFlight:    w.InFlight + 1,
			// TwoAtOnce: the Ask in the step is never answered.
			Lost: w.Lost || (w.Runner == Busy && w.Cur.Kind == Ask),
		}}
	case Drop:
		// A tick or a result of an ended entry is dropped.
		if w.Runner != Busy || !stale(c, w) {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Runner: Idle, InFlight: w.InFlight - 1, Cur: noEnv()}}
	case DefectEnds:
		// A defect of the work ends the actor, whatever its epoch, as Done
		// does.
		if w.Runner != Busy || w.Cur.Kind != Defect || w.StopReq {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: stopChildren(World{..drained(w),
			Runner:   Ended,
			Open:     false,
			Pending:  false,
			AfterEnd: w.AfterEnd || w.DoneSeen,
			Cur:      noEnv(),
			InFlight: w.InFlight - 1,
			EndBy:    ByDefect,
		})}
	case StepIt as st:
		return stepIt(c, w, st.D)
	case Arm as r:
		// The new entry arms its timer and starts its work, or has none,
		// once the old children ended (ArmEarly: the timer at once;
		// WorkEarly: the work at once), and then observers see it.
		// WorkBeforeCommit starts the work with the epoch before the
		// commit.
		if !w.Pending || w.Runner == Ended || (c.M != ArmEarlyMutant && w.Timer != NoChild) || (c.M != WorkEarlyMutant && w.Work != NoChild) {
			return None
		}
		let arms = if r.Timer { w.ArmsNow + 1 } else { w.ArmsNow }
		let starts = if r.Work { w.StartsNow + 1 } else { w.StartsNow }
		Some[World]{Value: showWritten(World{..w,
			ArmEarly:   w.ArmEarly || w.Timer != NoChild,
			WorkEarly:  w.WorkEarly || (r.Work && w.Work != NoChild),
			Timer:      if r.Timer { Sleeping } else { w.Timer },
			TimerEpoch: if r.Timer { 0 } else { w.TimerEpoch },
			ArmsNow:    if arms > 2 { 2 } else { arms },
			Work:       if r.Work { Running } else { w.Work },
			WorkEpoch:  if !r.Work { w.WorkEpoch } else { if c.M == WorkBeforeCommitMutant { -1 } else { 0 } },
			StartsNow:  if starts > 2 { 2 } else { starts },
			Pending:    false,
			Seen:       0,
		})}
	case RequestStop:
		// Stop from outside: admission closes at once.
		if w.StopReq {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, StopReq: true, Open: false}}
	case Halt:
		// The interrupted runner ends: an Ask in its step and every queued
		// Ask are answered Stopped; a state written before the stop is
		// shown.
		if !w.StopReq || w.Runner == Ended {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: showWritten(stopChildren(World{..drained(w),
			Runner:   Ended,
			InFlight: 0,
			Cur:      noEnv(),
			Pending:  false,
			EndBy:    ByStop,
		}))}
	case Subscribe as s:
		// An observer begins a Changes loop, at any point: its first state
		// is the one shown now (StaleSnapshot: the one before it).
		let i = obIx(s.O)
		let o = w.Obs[i]
		if o.Sub {
			return None
		}
		let first = if c.M == StaleSnapshotMutant && w.Shown > 0 { w.Shown - 1 } else { w.Shown }
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Obs: setObs(w.Obs, i, Obs{..o, Sub: true, Next: w.Shown, Buf: []int{first}})}}
	case Observe as s:
		// An observer reads its next state (NotifyTwice: it is read and
		// kept).
		let i = obIx(s.O)
		let o = w.Obs[i]
		if !o.Sub || o.Done || len(o.Buf) == 0 {
			return None
		}
		let v = o.Buf[0]
		let mut rest = []int{}
		for j, x in o.Buf {
			if j > 0 || c.M == NotifyTwiceMutant {
				rest = rest.Append(x)
			}
		}
		let count = if c.Ghost == LongObserverWitness && o.Count < 3 { o.Count + 1 } else { o.Count }
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w,
			ChangesBad: w.ChangesBad || v != o.Next,
			WaitForBad: w.WaitForBad || (!o.Read && v != o.Next),
			Obs:        setObs(w.Obs, i, Obs{..o, Next: o.Next + 1, Read: true, Count: count, Buf: rest}),
		}}
	case ObserverEnds as s:
		// An observer's loop ends once the actor ended and it read every
		// state shown to it (SkipBeforeStop: at the end, with states
		// unread).
		let i = obIx(s.O)
		let o = w.Obs[i]
		if !o.Sub || o.Done || w.Runner != Ended || (c.M != SkipBeforeStopMutant && len(o.Buf) != 0) {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Obs: setObs(w.Obs, i, Obs{..o, Done: true})}}
	case RequestDrain:
		// Drain closes admission; the runner goes on stepping what is
		// queued (DrainDrops: the last queued signal is dropped).
		if w.DrainReq || w.StopReq {
			return None
		}
		let drop = c.M == DrainDropsMutant && len(w.Inbox) > 0
		let last = if drop { w.Inbox[len(w.Inbox)-1] } else { noEnv() }
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w,
			DrainReq: true,
			Open:     false,
			Inbox:    if drop { removeAt(w.Inbox, len(w.Inbox)-1) } else { w.Inbox },
			Dropped:  w.Dropped || isSignal(last),
			Lost:     w.Lost || last.Kind == Ask,
		}}
	case DrainEnds:
		// A drained runner ends when nothing is queued and no step or entry
		// is open.
		if !w.DrainReq || w.StopReq || w.Runner != Idle || w.Pending || len(w.Inbox) != 0 {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: stopChildren(World{..w, Runner: Ended, EndBy: ByDrain})}
	case GiveOut:
		// OutputLate: the sink gets the owed outputs once the entry opened.
		if len(w.Owed) == 0 || w.Pending || w.Runner == Ended {
			return None
		}
		Some[World]{Value: World{..w, Owed: []int{}}}
	}
}

// stepIt is the step of the envelope in the step deciding d. Enter and
// Emit end the entry: its timer child is asked to stop, its work is
// interrupted, and the new entry's children wait for their end (Arm). Stay
// keeps the entry (StayRestarts restarts the timer). Done ends the actor
// (NoClose: the actor goes on). PublishFirst shows observers the new entry
// at the commit. Enter, Stay and Emit write the next state: a Stay's is
// shown at once, an entry's once its children run (Arm). An Emit's output
// is given here (OutputLate: owed until GiveOut).
func stepIt(c Cfg, w World, d Dec) Option[World] {
	if w.Runner != Busy || stale(c, w) || w.StopReq || w.Cur.Kind == Defect {
		return None
	}
	let mut commit = false
	let mut reenter = false
	let mut stay = false
	let mut emit = false
	let mut done = false
	match d {
	case DEnter:
		commit = true
		reenter = true
	case DEmit:
		commit = true
		reenter = true
		emit = true
	case DStay:
		commit = true
		stay = true
	case DDone:
		done = true
	case _:
	}
	if commit && w.State >= MaxWrites {
		return None
	}
	let tagged = w.Cur.Kind == Tick || w.Cur.Kind == Result
	let n = if c.M == AnswerTwiceMutant { 2 } else { 1 }
	let w1 = answered(World{..w,
		StaleBad: w.StaleBad || (tagged && w.Cur.Epoch != 0),
		AfterEnd: w.AfterEnd || w.DoneSeen,
		Cur:      noEnv(),
		InFlight: w.InFlight - 1,
	}, w.Cur, n)
	if done && c.M != NoCloseMutant {
		return Some[World]{Value: stopChildren(World{..drained(w1), Runner: Ended, Open: false, Pending: false, EndBy: ByDone})}
	}
	let restart = reenter || (stay && c.M == StayRestartsMutant)
	let s = if commit { w.State + 1 } else { w.State }
	let w2 = World{..w1,
		Runner:     Idle,
		Timer:      if restart && w.Timer == Sleeping { Stopping } else { w.Timer },
		Work:       if reenter && w.Work == Running { Stopping } else { w.Work },
		Inbox:      if reenter { aged(w.Inbox) } else { w.Inbox },
		TimerEpoch: if reenter { -1 } else { w.TimerEpoch },
		WorkEpoch:  if reenter { -1 } else { w.WorkEpoch },
		ArmsNow:    if reenter { 0 } else { w.ArmsNow },
		ArmsBad:    w.ArmsBad || (reenter && w.ArmsNow > 1),
		StartsNow:  if reenter { 0 } else { w.StartsNow },
		StartsBad:  w.StartsBad || (reenter && w.StartsNow > 1),
		Pending:    restart || w.Pending,
		Seen:       if reenter { if c.M == PublishFirstMutant { 0 } else { -1 } } else { w.Seen },
		DoneSeen:   w.DoneSeen || done,
		State:      s,
		Emits:      if c.Ghost == EmitSeenWitness && emit { setBool(w.Emits, s, true) } else { w.Emits },
		Owed:       if emit && c.M == OutputLateMutant { w.Owed.Append(s) } else { w.Owed },
	}
	if stay {
		return Some[World]{Value: publish(w2, s)}
	}
	Some[World]{Value: w2}
}

// stepWith is the step of the machine c.
func stepWith(c Cfg, s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	match s {
	case Boot:
		match a {
		case Start as b:
			Enter[St]{Next: Live{W: booted(b.Timer, b.Work)}}
		case _:
			Ignore
		}
	case Live as l:
		match next(c, l.W, a) {
		case None:
			Ignore
		case Some[World] as n:
			let v = canon(c, n.Value)
			let why = broken(c, v)
			if why != "" {
				Enter[St]{Next: Broken{Why: why}}
			} else {
				Enter[St]{Next: Live{W: v}}
			}
		}
	case _:
		Ignore
	}
}

func design(n int) Cfg {
	Cfg{M: NoMutant, Senders: n, Ghost: 0, Only: ""}
}

func mutant(m int, only string) Cfg {
	Cfg{M: m, Senders: 2, Ghost: 0, Only: only}
}

func stepDesign2(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] { stepWith(design(2), s, a) }
func stepDesign3(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] { stepWith(design(3), s, a) }

// The design keeps every invariant in the scope, with 2 senders and with 3.
type Design2 machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepDesign2,

	law Safe never reaches Broken,
}

type Design3 machine[St, Act] {
	initial: first(),
	step:    stepDesign3,

	law Safe never reaches Broken,
}

func stepNoEpoch(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	stepWith(mutant(NoEpochMutant, "NoStaleStep"), s, a)
}
func stepArmEarly(s St, a Act) Decision[St, string] {
	stepWith(mutant(ArmEarlyMutant, "ExitBeforeEntry"), s, a)
}
